Mike Hatz (mhatz@nyx10.cs.du.edu) wrote:
> I need some help figuring out how to put the X-Disclaimer line in Elm on 
> an Ultrix box and under plain old VMS mail on a VAX.  You know the line 
> that says "B&B inc. says opinions are not ours only our butthead 
> employees...".  Thanks.  Also can this be forced on the plain old 
> Berkeley /bin/mail program too?  Thanks.

It's called the "signature".
See the "Signature FAQ" which is posted to news.newusers.questions
twice every week, and the elm man page for the details. In short:
Create the file .signature with your favorite editor (not more
than 4 lines, please!).
Create the file .elm/elmrc by o (options) > (save) in elm
and then insert the line  signature=$HOME/.signature into this file
as told by the comment lines.

