OpenVMS is cuurently developing a new technology for applications which will 
allow them to be installed, removed, and packaged in a new and better manner
than is curretnly provided with the VMSINSTAL technology. This new technology
is call the "POLYCENTER Software Installation" utility, PCSI. This technology
will be distributed and documented with OpenVMS VAX and AXP Version 6.1.

For application developers that would like to investigate this technology, 
Digital is making available a draft version of the POLYCENTER Software 
Installation Developer's Guide via Digital's Internet gateway system. The manual
describes how to package software products including the description language,
product description files, product text files, and other relevant concepts.
The final version of the manual will be made available with the V6.1 releases. 
Information in this draft manaul is subject to change.

This manual compliments the POLYCENTER Software Installation Utility User's 
Guide which describes the tasks that system managers perform using the 
POLYCENTER Software Installation Utility. A draft of this manual is currently 
available on the on the OpenVMS AXP Software Developer's Toolkit.

Please note that OpenVMS will continue to support and distribute VMSINSTAL) 


