Your local bookstore should have plenty of books on SQL.  Find one
of these that covers embedded SQL -- Rdb uses standard SQL.  I
often use _Using SQL_ by James R. Groff & Paul N Weinberg, but any
book that covers SQL-92 should be fine.  This probably won't cover
dynamic SQL if you intend to use that or SQL modules.  You might
also be able to find a book on the language you intend to use (e.g.
COBOL) that has a chapter on using embedded SQL.  Remember too,
that you can always go into interactive SQL and use help.

You really should, however, have access to the Rdb doc set.  This
is especially true if you are going to use Rdb extentions to the
SQL-92 standard(like dynamic SQL or SQL modules or try to execute
DDL statements from an application).



